    "text": "<p> We see that the <code>javac</code> command fails if we make a syntax error:</p>\n\n<pre><code class=\"language-no-highlight\">$ javac HasAMainMethod.java\nHasAMainMethod.java:2: error: ';' expected\n  public static void main(String[] args) // removed a curly brace\n                                        ^\nHasAMainMethod.java:5: error: class, interface, or enum expected\n}\n^\n2 errors</code></pre>\n\n<p>Let's go back to the program that “worked”, which is still a bit odd, because it didn't produce any output at all when we ran it:</p>\n\n<p><iframe height=\"580px\" scrolling=\"yes\" src=\"https://tech.io/playground-widget/7bbf6639bba4749e3b684a5712ba076220785/welcome/1090860/HasAMainMethod\" width=\"100%\"></iframe></p>\n\n<pre><code>$ javac HasAMainMethod.java \n$ java HasAMainMethod\n$</code></pre>\n\n<p>Let's reflect on this code a little bit.</p>\n\n<h3><span style=\"color: #cc0000;\">Do Now! </span>Which of the following pieces of the <code>main()</code> method have we <em>not</em> seen before in this book?</h3>",
